":"Native CWI currently normalizes several malformed requests before SDK validation and loses structured error fields across the extension transport. This change validates the original request with the SDK before permission checks or normalization, preserves transport error fields, and keeps the content-side canonical SDK classes intact.\n\nThe native lab also exposed four dependency defects. Source-owned Bun patches now count the current unsigned action once against a standing allowance while retaining every other reservation; keep valid long basket names within permission-tag limits; honor a distinct certificate key revealer during acquisition and disclosure; and hydrate known transaction inputs from bound retained/storage evidence, aborting reservations when construction fails. Dependency versions remain pinned, and ESM/CJS declarations and source maps stay coherent.\n\nValidation on head7e39006: clean Bun1.2.10 frozen install;147 tests/867 assertions; typecheck and formatting; all four extension bundles and build verification. Regression tests execute the exported managers, Wallet/BEEF construction and real certificate cryptography. The new CI artifact will be admitted separately into TPNIL; these local checks are not a native qualification or a released-wallet claim.\n\nThe lab's original failed run and results remain unchanged. Full BRC100 conformance is not claimed; the remaining standards ambiguities and unsupported native coverage remain explicit.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-12T02:20:14Z","updated_at":"2026-11-12T07:00:12Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"8e7e5d152b93078e6c8f55680d3dcb73d2df5e6c","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"ty-everett:codex/native-wallet-validation-20261111","ref":"codex/native-wallet-validation-20261111","repo":{"id":1364972470,"node_id":"R_kgDOUVvTtg","name":"yours-wallet","full_name":"ty-everett/your